  <Note>A heriditary autosomal recessive disorder caused by mutations in the high-affinity carnitine transporter (SLC22A5 gene) that is expressed in muscle, heart, kidney, LYMPHOBLASTS, and FIBROBLASTS. This results in impaired fatty acid oxidation in skeletal and heart muscle. Renal wasting of carnitine results in low serum levels and diminished hepatic uptake of carnitine . It can be treated by supplementation of carnitine in early stages, but will result in lethal heart failure if untreated. OMIM: 212140
  </Note>
